# The board's security switch. Off (0) by default, as FRC robots run: the
# computer on the board's USB cable can restart it or put it in USB boot over
# the identity endpoint (BOARD_USB_ACTIONS, identity.env), and Atlas has a raw
# root console on the gadget's second serial port (ttyGS1). Whoever holds that
# cable can already reflash the board, so neither adds access off the cable.
# Off, orion-node also listens on 0.0.0.0:9200 with peer auth optional,
# status and live streams are open to read, and operators on the USB cable's
# network are enrolled for reboot, usb-boot and locate (orion-env).
# 1 turns all of it off: only SSH (with a key) and enrolled Orion operators
# manage the board (peer auth required), and ttyGS1 has no console. A change
# restarts orion-node (board-security.path). An OS sets it in /etc/board/security.env; a board's
# own choice goes in /data/board/security.env.
BOARD_SECURITY=0
